# Ship via PR (agent does the git)

Never push straight to `master`/`main`. Never ask Ammon to type git commands.

When finishing work that should land in the repo:

1. Create a new descriptive branch from the latest default branch
2. Commit with a clear message
3. Push with `-u`
4. Open a PR with `gh pr create` and return the URL

Ammon's job is one plain-English request (the change + that it should ship). Review + merge is human. Opt out only if he says so ("local only", "don't commit", "don't PR").

Do not force-push to shared branches. Do not amend pushed commits unless explicitly asked.
